-- title:
--   Quasi-inverse isogeny and transported embedding of 𝒪_D-endomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a commutative ring $\mathcal O$ with an element $\pi$, and a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ such that the ideal of $Onr$ generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal, and such that $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$; let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(r)$ — that is, a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $\Phi.F$ with an action $a \mapsto \Phi.\mathrm{act}\,a$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2} = W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$ by endomorphisms, additive and multiplicative in $a$, together with an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = [r]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \sigma(a)\circ\varpi$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$ — and assume $\Phi$ has height $4$, i.e. $\Phi.\mathrm{act}\,r$ has kernel of degree $r^4$. Let $X_0$ be such a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(\pi)$, let $\kappa : Onr/(\pi) \to Onr/(r)$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the two quotient maps out of $Onr$, let $n_0 \in \mathbb N$, and let $\beta_0$ be a pair of power series in two variables over $Onr/(r)$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change $X_0\otimes_\kappa$ (an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism, i.e. a homomorphism of formal groups commuting with the action and with $\varpi$, whose kernel has degree $r^{4n_0}$). Finally let $E_0$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the centralizer of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{act}\,a\}_a \cup \{\Phi.\varpi\}$ inside $\mathrm{End}(\Phi.F)$ into $M_2(K_0)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $N_0 \in \mathbb N$, a series pair $\beta_0'$ and an injective ring homomorphism $E_X$ from the centralizer of $\{X_0.\mathrm{act}\,a\}_a \cup \{X_0.\varpi\}$ inside $\mathrm{End}(X_0.F)$ into $M_2(K_0)$, such that $\beta_0'$ is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism from $X_0\otimes_\kappa$ to $\Phi$ with $\beta_0'\circ\beta_0 = \Phi.\mathrm{act}(r^{N_0})$ and $\beta_0\circ\beta_0' = (X_0\otimes_\kappa).\mathrm{act}(r^{N_0})$, and such that every $\varepsilon$ in the centralizer for $X_0$ admits an $e$ in the centralizer for $\Phi$ whose power series equals $\beta_0'\circ(\kappa_*\varepsilon)\circ\beta_0$ and which satisfies $E_0 e = r^{N_0}\cdot E_X\varepsilon$ in $M_2(K_0)$.
--
--   This is the transport of a matrix embedding of the $\mathcal O_D$-endomorphism algebra along a quasi-isogeny between special formal modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting: a quasi-inverse $\beta_0'$ to $\beta_0$ is produced, and conjugation by it carries endomorphisms of $X_0$ to endomorphisms of $\Phi$, compatibly with the given embedding up to the factor $r^{N_0}$. It is used in the rigidification of fake elliptic curves, where the resulting embedding $E_X$ at the Drinfeld frame feeds the comparison of rigidified deformation data over Artinian and local base rings.
